From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joey Arhar <jarhar@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 13:18:16 -0700
Subject: Synchronize form control autofill state with suggested values

Previously, HTMLFormControlElement::autofill_state_ could become
desynchronized from the rendered suggestion state (suggested_option_ on
HTMLSelectElement and suggested_value_ on TextControlElement) when DOM
operations reset autofill_state_ to kNotFilled without clearing the
suggestion:

- On HTMLSelectElement, operations like self-assigning
  select.selectedIndex or form.reset() reset autofill_state_ to
  kNotFilled without clearing suggested_option_ or closing the preview
  popover.
- On TextControlElement (HTMLInputElement and HTMLTextAreaElement),
  operations like setting input.checked or input.defaultChecked called
  SetAutofillState(kNotFilled) without clearing suggested_value_, which
  re-enabled field-sizing:content sizing on the previewed suggestion
  text. Additionally, self-assigning textarea.value returned early
  before updating autofill_state_.

This change makes HTMLFormControlElement::SetAutofillState() virtual and
overrides it in both HTMLSelectElement and TextControlElement so that
transitioning autofill_state_ away from a previewed/filled state clears
any active suggested_option_ or suggested_value_. Because
SetAutofillState() now clears the suggestion when resetting to
kNotFilled, SetSuggestedValue() and SetSuggestedOption() are updated to
set suggested_value_ and suggested_option_ before calling
SetAutofillState() to avoid infinite recursion when clearing a
suggestion. It also ensures HTMLTextAreaElement::SetValueCommon()
updates autofill_state_ before its early return when the value is
unchanged, and replaces the temporary FindBuffer popover check with a
CHECK.

Fixed: 556233596, 562224383, 562225118
Change-Id: I3decec2a1dab8029d9c275c0bbc5e0b8b47c478b
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8480911
Reviewed-by: Joey Arhar <jarhar@chromium.org>
Reviewed-by: Kent Tamura <tkent@chromium.org>
